From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adeeb Shihadeh <adeeb@comma.ai>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 03:46:09 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: power: reset: qcom,pshold: add
 qcom,no-firmware-warm-reset

Some Qualcomm secure firmware implements PSCI without SYSTEM_RESET2, and
its SYSTEM_RESET is a cold reset. On such boards the only way to restart
without losing RAM (pstore, crash logs, a download-mode request) is to
drop PS_HOLD with the PMIC configured for a warm reset.

This can't be probed: PSCI_FEATURES reports SYSTEM_RESET2 missing, but not
whether SYSTEM_RESET is warm or cold. Add a property that describes this
firmware behaviour, so the restart driver can take warm restarts through
PS_HOLD on these boards only.

Signed-off-by: Adeeb Shihadeh <adeeb@comma.ai>
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/power/reset/qcom,pshold.yaml      | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/reset/qcom,pshold.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/reset/qcom,pshold.yaml
index 527962d54a..c752b06e0e 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/reset/qcom,pshold.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/reset/qcom,pshold.yaml
@@ -21,6 +21,14 @@ properties:
   reg:
     maxItems: 1
 
+  qcom,no-firmware-warm-reset:
+    type: boolean
+    description:
+      The secure firmware has no warm reset. PSCI SYSTEM_RESET2 is not
+      implemented, and SYSTEM_RESET is a cold reset, which loses the contents
+      of RAM. Warm restarts have to drop PS_HOLD with the PMIC set up for a
+      warm reset.
+
 required:
   - compatible
   - reg
